.TH HSH 1 "May 2026" "Holberton School" "Simple Shell Manual"
.SH NAME
.B hsh
\- a simple UNIX command interpreter
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ./hsh
.PP
.B echo
"command" |
.B ./hsh
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hsh
is a simple shell that reads commands from standard input or
from a script, and executes them. It mimics the behavior of
.B /bin/sh
with a limited set of features.
.PP
The shell supports both interactive and non-interactive modes.
In interactive mode, a prompt
.B $
is displayed before each command.
.SH INVOCATION
Run the shell in interactive mode:
.PP
.B $ ./hsh
.PP
Or in non-interactive mode:
.PP
.B $ echo "ls" | ./hsh
.SH BUILTIN COMMANDS
.TP
.B exit
Exits the shell.
.TP
.B env
Prints the current environment variables.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Run a command with full path:
.B $ /bin/ls
.TP
Run using PATH:
.B $ ls
